  "findings": [
    "CriticalSingularBoundary gives p=9 or z=0 -> singular minor -> Fourier family; requires current-model adaptation of singular classification.",
    "SingularFourierRouting needs Worker12.ZeroClassification plus the existing generic H2 obstruction for Tao. No numerical atlas endpoint is needed for the logical routing.",
    "ZeroClassification reuses the existing Hadamard6 singular_corner_hasRepeatedRowOrColumn; no new singular-corner algebra should be written.",
    "ZeroRowTransport/ZeroExtraction reuse generic embeddingPermutation, coordinate roundtrips and isHadamard transports already checked. The archived families classification requires cubic endpoints, whose finite witnesses must be reused, not regenerated.",
    "Worker12.ZeroPattern duplicates literal_fourier3_isHadamard already extracted into FourierRoutingModel. Reuse existing theorem and current row-Gram helper.",
    "AllFourBlocks/ExactFourierPresentation and the finite cubic classification are separate remaining dependencies, not counted as proved by the current geometric route.",
    "Exceptional z=-3 and z=-2 give p=0 and p=5, already the alternatives in the checked strip counting obstruction. They may be retained in the final scalar case split; separate full family classifications for those values are not necessarily required.",
    "Nonzero-J still needs the full reduction with physical denominator guards discharged and common exceptional p value established.",
    "Atlas excluded. No sources from this read-only singular route have been adopted or certified."
  ],
